config CACHE_NXP_LLC
	bool "NXP CodaCache last-level cache driver"
	default y
	depends on SOC_SERIES_IMXRT266X
	depends on EXTERNAL_CACHE
	select CACHE_HAS_DRIVER
	help
	  Enable the NXP two-level cache backend for i.MX RT266x (MIMXRT2660).
	  This single drivers/cache backend serves BOTH cache levels behind
	  Zephyr's level-less cache API: the Cortex-M85 L1 (via the CMSIS SCB
	  helpers) and the CodaCache last-level cache (LLC) in front of the XSPI
	  external-memory windows. Selecting EXTERNAL_CACHE removes the arch
	  Cortex-M L1 backend (arch/arm/core/cortex_m/cache.c, gated on
	  ARCH_CACHE) from the build, so this driver must cover both levels.
	  DMA buffers must NOT live in the LLC-cached XSPI aliases (0x68000000 /
	  0x88000000): eDMA masters bypass the LLC, the LLC line (128 bytes) is
	  wider than CONFIG_DCACHE_LINE_SIZE, and there is no invalidate that
	  skips write-back. Keep DMA buffers in on-chip SRAM, TCM, or the direct
	  XSPI windows (0x60000000 / 0x80000000). __nocache over a cached alias
	  does not reach the XSPI and must not be used there.
